        ]
      ],
      "id": "faus2pz"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "9uan06p",
      "content": "Formed by C.R. Das and Motilal Nehru after withdrawal of Non-Cooperation. Aim: Enter councils and obstruct colonial governance."
    },
    {
      "id": "9ov6ev1",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "4. COMMUNAL AWARD (1932)"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "xnq5sup",
      "content": "Announced by Ramsay MacDonald providing separate electorates to minorities including Depressed Classes; led to Poona Pact."
    },
    {
      "id": "vrltwef",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "5. INDIVIDUAL SATYAGRAHA (1940)"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "xm7tdv0",
      "content": "Launched by Gandhi against August Offer. First Satyagrahi: Vinoba Bhave; Second: Jawaharlal Nehru."
    },
    {
      "id": "xxrtp75",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "6. FORWARD BLOC (1939)"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "v7y7uze",
      "content": "Formed by Subhash Chandra Bose after resigning from Congress presidency due to ideological differences."
    },
    {
      "id": "6wm4132",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "7. DIRECT ACTION DAY (16 August 1946)"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "mt545ai",
      "content": "Called by Muslim League demanding Pakistan; led to communal riots in Calcutta."
    },
    {
      "id": "259vh56",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "8. SHIMLA CONFERENCE (1945)"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "dct994c",
      "content": "Based on Wavell Plan; failed due to disagreement between Congress and Muslim League."
    },
    {
      "type": "examAlert",
      "items": [
        "Memorize the chronological sequence of pre-Congress acts: Vernacular Press Act (1878) followed by the Ilbert Bill Controversy (1883) and the Formation of INC (1885).",
        "Focus on 1940s milestones for direct timeline questions: August Offer (1940), Lahore Resolution (1940), Shimla Conference (1945), and Direct Action Day (16 August 1946)."
      ],
      "id": "u7o6lt8"
    },
    {
      "id": "ij330ng",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "9. AUGUST OFFER (1940)"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "cb42ti9",
      "content": "British promise of post-war dominion status; rejected by Congress."
    },
    {
      "id": "tq24c9z",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "10. LAHORE RESOLUTION (1940)"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "0ies7tj",
      "content": "Muslim League formally demanded separate nation (Pakistan)."
    },
    {
      "id": "ba7lgy3",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "11. PEASANT & WORKER MOVEMENTS"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "vnqdiow",
      "content": "Kisan Sabhas, Tebhaga Movement (1946), Telangana Movement (1946–51), and Trade Union growth strengthened mass politics."
    },
